From c0235eff650720faff05452a06a0a09479b3621f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:31:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] freedreno/a5xx: program the 2D source and use BLIT_OP_SCALE

On a512 a 2D blit does nothing whatsoever: the destination keeps
whatever it held before, and no fault or error is raised. On a530 it
mostly works, but a converting blit such as r16f to rg16f comes back
wrong. It looks like a512 (and maybe other GPUs) silently ignores
CP_BLIT(BLIT_OP_COPY), but perform no actual operation without reporting
any error to the caller side. The packet is consumed, the CP runs on
past it, the 2D registers read back exactly as programmed, but no memory
transaction is issued.

Describe missing registers and program them, and ask for BLIT_OP_SCALE.
Both CP_BLIT sites need it: the buffer path describes its source as the
single row of R8_UNORM it copies.

BLIT_OP_SCALE converts through the intermediate format, so a snorm copy
would turn -128 into -127. Blit snorm formats as the matching unorm
one, as a6xx does.

Measured against u_blitter over every identity pair of 20 renderable
formats, with the destination pre-filled so an untouched buffer cannot
be mistaken for a correct result: a512 goes from 0/20 to 20/20 and a530
from 19/20 to 20/20, r16f to rg16f being the pair a530 gained.

